#
# SGLang v0.5.17 + our SM121 build patches. Next line, NOT YET BUILT and NOT
# GPU-VALIDATED — production stays on sglang-0.5.16-sm121.recipe (the recipe
# behind default_sglang_image) until this one has been through the acceptance
# gate and a real serving run. Created 2026-08-09 to evaluate the v0.5.17 line
# (released 2026-08-08, 582 PRs / 194 contributors).
#
# THE HEADLINE: the sgl-kernel TREE MOVED. RFC #29630 ("sweep dedicated kernels
# into kernels.ops") finished in v0.5.17 and relocated the entire top-level
#   sgl-kernel/            ->  python/sglang/kernels/aot/
# The package itself is untouched (name "sglang-kernel", version 0.4.5, same
# CMakeLists.txt / Makefile / csrc layout, still EXCLUDED from the sglang wheel
# in python/pyproject.toml, so it is still built as its own wheel). But every
# hardcoded `sgl-kernel/` path breaks, in BOTH directions:
#   * our four CMakeLists patches carry the old path in their diff headers, and
#   * the upstream scitrera Dockerfile.sglang-nightly itself does
#     `sed -i ... sgl-kernel/pyproject.toml` and `cd sgl-kernel && uv build`.
#     Note scitrera has NOT tracked SGLang past 0.5.12 in their own recipes, so
#     nothing upstream will fix this for us.
# Hence the two NEW knobs below, SGL_KERNEL_DIR + SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT.
# Without them the build dies at `cd sgl-kernel` after the (expensive) clone.
#
# ── DELTA vs sglang-0.5.16-sm121.recipe ─────────────────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.16 → 0.5.17, SGLANG_REF → v0.5.17.
#   2. SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot (NEW KNOB, empty/absent in every
#      older recipe = "sgl-kernel", i.e. byte-identical behaviour). Passed to the
#      Dockerfile as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR and consumed in three places: the
#      SGLANG_VERSION sed on the kernel pyproject, the four post-apply
#      `grep -q '<marker>' <dir>/CMakeLists.txt` verifications, and the `cd`
#      of the wheel build. See patches/dockerfile-sm121.patch item 10.
#   3. SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.17" (NEW KNOB). Selects the four repathed
#      CMakeLists patches; apply_patches() installs them under the CANONICAL
#      names, so the Dockerfile step is unchanged. It WINS over
#      SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD (which stays 1 below purely as provenance: the
#      -v0.5.17 files carry the mainahead content).
#   4. FLASHINFER_VERSION 0.6.16 → 0.6.16.post3. See the block below.
#   5. TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT stays "-v0.5.16" — the FILE NAME is a generation
#      label, not a ref restriction; the variant was re-verified clean against
#      v0.5.17 (see PATCH VERIFY).
#   6. CUTLASS_DSL / TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS / BASE_IMAGE: UNCHANGED. v0.5.17's
#      pyproject is byte-identical to v0.5.16 on transformers (==5.12.1),
#      kernels (>=0.14.1,<0.15), nvidia-cutlass-dsl (==4.6.0, we stay at 4.6.1)
#      and torch (==2.11.0, we stay on the 2.12/cu132 base) — it only moved its
#      own flashinfer pin 0.6.14 → 0.6.15.post1, still two patch steps behind
#      ours. NO pytorch-base rebuild needed.
#      PyPI-latest for the record, all deliberately NOT taken: transformers
#      5.14.1 (no perf relevance, not in the inference hot path), kernels 0.16.0
#      (violates the upstream constraint), nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2/4.7.0 (4.7
#      is past the API window flashinfer #3922 migrated to; see the CUTLASS
#      block), huggingface_hub 1.27.0 (our 1.26.0 FLOOR already carries the fix).
#   7. Upstream dependency bumps that ride along with the ref (informational,
#      none of them a knob here): sgl-deep-gemm 0.1.4.post1 → 0.1.5.post1,
#      helion 0.2.6 → 1.4, mooncake 0.3.12.post1, dynamo-tokenizers 1.7.0.
#      tilelang stays 0.1.11.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-08-09, non-GPU, dry-run vs raw v0.5.17 source) ────────
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.17.patch           clean (regenerated, 2 hunks)
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-v0.5.17.patch          clean (regenerated, 1 hunk)
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-v0.5.17.patch     clean (regenerated, 4 hunks)
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla-v0.5.17.patch        clean (regenerated, 1 hunk)
#      All four regenerated with ZERO fuzz/offset by applying the old ones at
#      the new path in build order and re-diffing, so they are not just the old
#      files with a rewritten header. Verified to apply in sequence
#      (arch-prune → disable-fa3 → skip-sm90-target → skip-flashmla) and to
#      leave all 8 'dgxarley ...' markers in the file. The CANONICAL (old-path)
#      files correctly FAIL on this ref, so a recipe that forgets
#      SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT aborts loudly instead of building unpatched.
#   ✅ sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch          applies (hunk 1417, offset -29)
#   ✅ sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  clean (path
#      python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py still exists)
#   ✅ Dockerfile chain re-verified against pristine scitrera origin/main after
#      regenerating dockerfile-sm121.patch: sm121 → kernels-pin → audio-deps →
#      cutlass-dsl-pin → accelerate → dsv4-flashmla → dsv4-mtp-marlin-tilelang →
#      hf-hub-floor, all apply.
#   ❌ sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                        target still gone → GATED OFF
#      (unchanged from v0.5.16, PR #30448).
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/) NOT yet run against
#      a built image. STATIC pre-check 2026-08-09: all 38 target module paths
#      referenced by the patch set still exist at v0.5.17, INCLUDING p34's
#      v0.5.16 alt-target srt/mem_cache/kv_cache_configurator.py — so unlike the
#      0.5.16 bump there is no known relocation. That says nothing about the
#      ANCHOR STRINGS. Run scripts/verify_sglang_image.sh (bare / glm / hy3)
#      before serving anything: drift is logged as a warning and never crashes
#      the pod, so a deploy would SILENTLY run without the affected fixes.
#   B. INHERITED from v0.5.16, still open: moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton
#      for NVFP4 is gone (#30448) — nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass) and
#      Minimax-M2.5 @ PP=4 (triton) need re-testing or re-pinning; and
#      compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True
#      ASSERTS instead of running. See TURBOQUANT.md.
#   C. NEW in v0.5.17, from the release's own "Breaking Changes" section:
#      * The FP8 per-tensor GEMM backend on SM120 switches to cuBLAS (#31961).
#        This is OUR arch family. Any FP8 (not NVFP4) profile is on a new
#        kernel path here — re-measure before trusting throughput numbers.
#      * sgl-kernel AOT bmm_fp8 is DELETED in favour of flashinfer.bmm_fp8, and
#        the AOT router GEMM + fused A GEMM are removed (#31202, #30280). Our
#        flashinfer pin is well past the version that provides it, but this is
#        the first ref where the AOT wheel no longer carries those symbols.
#      * UnifiedRadixTree default + QServe/FBGEMM removal (from v0.5.16) still
#        apply; nothing new on that front.
#   D. NEW, from the release's "Known Issues": the SM120 DeepGEMM release-pipeline
#      test is temporarily SKIPPED upstream (#32193), i.e. our arch family has
#      less CI coverage on this ref than on v0.5.16. And the FlashInfer
#      rmsnorm+quant fusion for SM90/SM100/SM120 was landed AND reverted this
#      cycle (#32994, #33455) — it is NOT in this release, so do not expect it.
#   E. flashinfer is again ahead of SGLang's own pin (0.6.15.post1). Rollback
#      order in the FLASHINFER_VERSION block.
#   F. INHERITED: NVFP4 ATTENTION on SM121 (flashinfer #3897) is still only
#      KERNEL-level verified (2026-07-28 on spark5), never validated end to end
#      through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model. Judge output quality by
#      pattern-grep + token distribution + tail, not by finish_reason.
#   G. SM120 work landed in v0.5.17 that we have NOT exercised: FP4 Indexer for
#      DeepSeek-V4 on SM120 (#27059), GLM-5.1 SM120 (#26928), GPT-OSS FlashInfer
#      MXFP4 on SM120 (#32668), FlashMLA page-split (#32320), DSV4/SM120 fused
#      MHC opt-in (#30954), scatter fallback (#31669). Several of these overlap
#      with what our p30-p35 DSA patches do by hand — check whether any of them
#      is now redundant BEFORE re-porting anchors (same lesson as the v0.5.16
#      fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch_sm120 absorption).
#
# Prerequisite: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132 present on the
# build host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, see ensure_base_image_present
# in build_sm121_image.sh).
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132

# flashinfer 0.6.16.post3 (2026-08-08). Patch bump over the 0.6.16 final that
# the 0.5.16 image ships; the whole 0.6.16 SM121 rationale from that recipe
# (#3897 NVFP4 attention on SM121, #3838 SM120 qk_correction/lse correctness,
# #3960 GDN CuteDSL as sm_121a on DGX Spark, #3922 cutlass-dsl 4.6 API
# migration) carries over UNCHANGED — the three post releases add no SM12x
# feature work at all. What they DO add (compare v0.6.16...v0.6.16.post3 is
# exactly 3 commits):
#   • post1 — release-branch bookkeeping, no functional delta vs 0.6.16.
#   • post2 — picks up the tvm-ffi v0.1.13-post2 ABI-compatibility hotfix.
#     THIS is the reason for the bump. tvm-ffi is the FFI layer every flashinfer
#     kernel binding loads through, and upstream explicitly recommends moving to
#     it ("We recommend upgrading to this latest version").
#   • post3 — reverts #3738 (SM90 CUTLASS MoE backend) + dependents #4025/#4080
#     on the release branch. Hopper-only path, inert on GB10.
# Wheels verified 2026-08-09 on https://flashinfer.ai/whl — all three packages
# exist at 0.6.16.post3, including the one that matters for arm64:
#   flashinfer-python    0.6.16.post3  (py3-none-any)
#   flashinfer-cubin     0.6.16.post3  (py3-none-any)   ← not on PyPI, only here
#   flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.16.post3+cu130 manylinux_2_28_aarch64
#
# NOT taken: 0.6.17. It exists only as RCs (rc5 as of 2026-08-08) and the
# stable-only pin policy from the 0.5.16 recipe stands. Worth taking the moment
# it goes final — it carries real SM12x work: #4117 GDN WY decode on SM121,
# #3903 trtllm_allreduce extended to SM12x, #4130 cute SM120 fused MoE (SwiGLU),
# #4253 mm_fp4 SM120 NVFP4 dense GEMM synced to b12x HEAD, #4161 xqa flaky-test
# fix "on spark".
#
# ⚠️  MUST re-run the GB10 rmsnorm smoke test on the built image (see the
#     CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION block): an ABI change in the FFI layer is precisely
#     the class of change that can turn the CuTe-DSL dispatch into a silent
#     CUDA-JIT fallback. Check _use_cuda_norm is False, not just that the
#     output is finite.
# Roll-back order: 0.6.16 (what 0.5.16-sm121 ships and is GPU-cleared on),
# then 0.6.15.post1 (live-validated on 0.5.15.post1-sm121), then 0.6.15.post1
# is also v0.5.17's own upstream pin.
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.15.post1
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16.post3

# transformers 5.12.1 — exactly v0.5.17's pyproject pin (==5.12.1, unchanged
# since v0.5.15). Do NOT bump past the SGLang ref (no perf benefit, transformers
# is not in the inference hot path; PyPI-latest 5.14.1 is irrelevant here).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 — exactly v0.5.17's constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unchanged). PyPI-latest 0.16.0 violates it. PERF-NEUTRAL on SM121: the only
# hub-loaded kernel (sgl-flash-attn3) is hard-disabled on GB10 and has no
# sm_121/ARM64 builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.1 — explicit pin, force-reinstalled late in the build.
# v0.5.17 still pins 4.6.0 upstream; flashinfer still requires only >=4.5.0
# (open-ended), and NVIDIA has shipped different wheel CONTENT under the same
# version number before (the 4.5.2 mlir_global_dtors 'data' ICE, see
# reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap) — the explicit pin stays mandatory.
# NOT taken: 4.6.2 / 4.7.0 (PyPI-latest). flashinfer #3922 migrated off the APIs
# removed in cutlass-dsl 4.6 while keeping 4.5.x compatibility; that makes 4.6.x
# the explicitly-supported window, and 4.7 is past it with nothing to gain.
# ⚠️  MUST GPU-verify on the built image before deploy (rmsnorm smoke test):
#   python -c "import flashinfer, torch; \
#     from flashinfer.norm import rmsnorm; \
#     x=torch.randn(4,512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     w=torch.randn(512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     print(rmsnorm(x,w).shape)"
# and confirm the DSL path is actually TAKEN (norm/__init__.py falls back to
# CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch, which makes the smoke
# test go green without ever compiling a DSL kernel):
#   _cute_dsl_supports_arch(12,1) / is_cute_dsl_arch_supported(12,1) → True
#   norm._use_cuda_norm(cuda:0) → False   ← False means DSL, not CUDA JIT
#   the *_cute symbols (rmsnorm_cute, fused_add_rmsnorm_cute, …) all import
# Fallback: 4.6.0 (the upstream pin), then 4.5.1 (last pre-swap release).
# CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.0
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.1

# Audio multimodal deps — see the 0.5.15.post1 recipe. SGLang pulls numba itself
# (numba==0.65.1); librosa is still needed (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate — baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader imports it).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

# huggingface_hub FLOOR (not an exact pin). Guards against the xet gated-repo
# download bug: hub PR #4394 (tree-listing cache) forwarded the REDACTED xetHash
# placeholder that the /tree API returns for GATED repos straight to hf_xet →
# "Task error: Unable to parse string as hex hash value" on every fresh
# snapshot_download of a gated model (hf_preload job, shard jobs, model-download
# initContainer). hf_xet was never at fault. Fixed by hub PR #4595, released in
# v1.26.0 (2026-07-30). See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md. Neither hub nor hf_xet
# is pinned anywhere else in the build, so without this floor an unlucky
# re-resolve could quietly reintroduce the crash the moment the cluster stops
# setting HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1. Installed as the LAST pip action of the builder
# stage (dockerfile-hf-hub-floor.patch) so nothing can downgrade it afterwards.
HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.17
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.17"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Kept at 1 for provenance — the -v0.5.17
# files below ARE the mainahead content (the mscclpp link refactor is still in
# the tree) — but SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT takes precedence in apply_patches(),
# so the -mainahead siblings themselves are not used on this ref.
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# ── NEW on v0.5.17: sgl-kernel tree relocation (RFC #29630) ──────────────────
# Suffix of the four CMakeLists source patches to install under the canonical
# names. "-v0.5.17" = same edits as -mainahead, regenerated at the new path with
# zero fuzz. Empty/absent in every older recipe → unchanged behaviour there.
SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.17"

# Where that tree now lives inside the sglang checkout, passed to the Dockerfile
# as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default "sgl-kernel", so older recipes are byte-
# identical). MUST match the path in the patch variant above.
SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-header patch: TARGET STILL GONE (PR #30448) → OFF ─────────
# python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh has not returned in
# v0.5.17 and cutlass_moe_fp4() is still absent; NVFP4 MoE runs through
# FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, the backend our model profiles pin
# anyway (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass). At 1 the in-container dry-run
# would abort the build. Consequence for the profiles: see OPEN RISK B above.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (native since v0.5.13) ──────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIVE since v0.5.14 (PR #25820) → OFF ───────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang indexer compat → ON ───────
# Unchanged rationale vs 0.5.16: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method still has
# no marlin branch for the MTP/nextn draft-MoE layers, and the TileLang uint8
# arg check still bites. Both source patches dry-run-verified against v0.5.17 on
# 2026-08-09 (marlin: hunk at 1417, offset -29; tilelang: clean).
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variant of the tilelang compat patch. "-v0.5.16" selects
# sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: the path introduced by RFC
# #29630 (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) and only the uint8-view hunk,
# because upstream adopted the 2D alloc_shared half. That file name is a
# GENERATION label, not a ref restriction — the path and the hunk are unchanged
# in v0.5.17, verified clean. apply_patches() installs the selected variant
# under the canonical name, so the Dockerfile step is unchanged.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) → OFF ──────────────────
# ⚠️  The OPEN dispatch fix #28099 is a RUNTIME patch in sglang_launch.sh and is
#     unaffected by this flag (p21/p22) — re-check Qwen3.6 live.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

IMAGE_TAG=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.17-sm121
